{"gatibudDipratyavasanarTasabdakarmakarmakaRamaRi karta": [{"id": "gatibudDipratyavasAnArTaSabdakarmAkarmakARAmaRi kartA", "headword": "गतिबुद्धिप्रत्यवसानार्थशब्दकर्माकर्मकाणामणि कर्ता", "headword_slp1": "gatibudDipratyavasAnArTaSabdakarmAkarmakARAmaRi kartA", "fold": "gatibudDipratyavasanarTasabdakarmakarmakaRamaRi karta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Of the verbs having the sense of 'motion', 'knowledge or information' and 'eating' and of verbs that have some literary work for their object and of intransitive verbs, that which was the agent of the verb in its primitive (non-णि or non-causal state), is called the कर्म or object, in its causative state (when the verb takes the affix णि).\n\nTerms: कारक-कर्म-संज्ञा", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गतिबुद्धिप्रत्यवसानार्थशब्दकर्माकर्मकाणामणि कर्ता १.४.५२", "१.४.५२", "१.४.५२ गतिबुद्धिप्रत्यवसानार्थशब्दकर्माकर्मकाणामणि कर्ता"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatibudDipratyavasAnArTaSabdakarmAkarmakARAmaRi kartA १.४.५२", "१.४.५२", "१.४.५२ gatibudDipratyavasAnArTaSabdakarmAkarmakARAmaRi kartA"]}], "gatisca": [{"id": "gatiSca", "headword": "गतिश्च", "headword_slp1": "gatiSca", "fold": "gatisca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The words प्र etc. are called also गति when in composition with a verb.\n\nTerms: उपसर्ग-संज्ञा", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गतिश्च १.४.६०", "१.४.६०", "१.४.६० गतिश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatiSca १.४.६०", "१.४.६०", "१.४.६० gatiSca"]}], "gatyarTakarmaRi dvitiyacaturTyO ceswayamanaDvani": [{"id": "gatyarTakarmaRi dvitIyAcaturTyO cezwAyAmanaDvani", "headword": "गत्यर्थकर्मणि द्वितीयाचतुर्थ्यौ चेष्टायामनध्वनि", "headword_slp1": "gatyarTakarmaRi dvitIyAcaturTyO cezwAyAmanaDvani", "fold": "gatyarTakarmaRi dvitiyacaturTyO ceswayamanaDvani", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the case of roots implying motion, the place which the motion is directed takes the affix of the 2nd (Accusative) or the 4th (Dative) case in denoting the 'object', when physical motion is meant and the object is not a word expressing 'road'.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-2, 4", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गत्यर्थकर्मणि द्वितीयाचतुर्थ्यौ चेष्टायामनध्वनि २.३.१२", "२.३.१२", "२.३.१२ गत्यर्थकर्मणि द्वितीयाचतुर्थ्यौ चेष्टायामनध्वनि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatyarTakarmaRi dvitIyAcaturTyO cezwAyAmanaDvani २.३.१२", "२.३.१२", "२.३.१२ gatyarTakarmaRi dvitIyAcaturTyO cezwAyAmanaDvani"]}], "gatisTaGupaBuByaH sicaH parasmEpadesu": [{"id": "gAtisTAGupABUByaH sicaH parasmEpadezu", "headword": "गातिस्थाघुपाभूभ्यः सिचः परस्मैपदेषु", "headword_slp1": "gAtisTAGupABUByaH sicaH parasmEpadezu", "fold": "gatisTaGupaBuByaH sicaH parasmEpadesu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "There is लुक् elision of the affix सिच् -- च्लेः सिच् ३.१.४४ in the prSmEpd after the verbs गा 'to go', स्था 'to stand', the verbs called घु मृषस्तितिक्षायाम् १.२.२०, पा 'to drink' and भू 'to be'.\n\nTerms: सिच्-elision", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गातिस्थाघुपाभूभ्यः सिचः परस्मैपदेषु २.४.७७", "२.४.७७", "२.४.७७ गातिस्थाघुपाभूभ्यः सिचः परस्मैपदेषु"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gAtisTAGupABUByaH sicaH parasmEpadezu २.४.७७", "२.४.७७", "२.४.७७ gAtisTAGupABUByaH sicaH parasmEpadezu"]}], "gatvarasca": [{"id": "gatvaraSca", "headword": "गत्वरश्च", "headword_slp1": "gatvaraSca", "fold": "gatvarasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "And the word गत्वर is irregularly formed.\n\nTerms: Irregular", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गत्वरश्च ३.२.१६४", "३.२.१६४", "३.२.१६४ गत्वरश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatvaraSca ३.२.१६४", "३.२.१६४", "३.२.१६४ gatvaraSca"]}], "gatyarTakarmakaslisasiNsTasavasajanaruhajiryatiByasca": [{"id": "gatyarTAkarmakaSlizaSINsTA''savasajanaruhajIryatiByaSca", "headword": "गत्यर्थाकर्मकश्लिषशीङ्स्थाऽऽसवसजनरुहजीर्यतिभ्यश्च", "headword_slp1": "gatyarTAkarmakaSlizaSINsTA''savasajanaruhajIryatiByaSca", "fold": "gatyarTakarmakaslisasiNsTasavasajanaruhajiryatiByasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix क्त is used in denoting the agent as well as the act and the object after verbs implying motion after intransitive roots and after the verbs 1. श्लिष् 'to embrace' 2. शि 'to lie down' 3. स्था 'to stand' 4. आस् 'to sit' 5. वस् 'to dwell' 6. जन् 'to produce' 7. रुह् 'to mount' 8. जृ 'to grow old'.\n\nTerms: क्त", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गत्यर्थाकर्मकश्लिषशीङ्स्थाऽऽसवसजनरुहजीर्यतिभ्यश्च ३.४.७२", "३.४.७२", "३.४.७२ गत्यर्थाकर्मकश्लिषशीङ्स्थाऽऽसवसजनरुहजीर्यतिभ्यश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatyarTAkarmakaSlizaSINsTA''savasajanaruhajIryatiByaSca ३.४.७२", "३.४.७२", "३.४.७२ gatyarTAkarmakaSlizaSINsTA''savasajanaruhajIryatiByaSca"]}], "gatiranantaraH": [{"id": "gatiranantaraH", "headword": "गतिरनन्तरः", "headword_slp1": "gatiranantaraH", "fold": "gatiranantaraH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A word called गति -- गतिश्च १.४.६०, when standing immediately before a Participle in क्त having a Passive significance, retains its accent.\n\nTerms: समास accent", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["गतिरनन्तरः ६.२.४९", "६.२.४९", "६.२.४९ गतिरनन्तरः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["gatiranantaraH ६.२.४९", "६.२.४९", "६.२.४९ gatiranantaraH"]}], "gatikarakopapadat‌ kft‌": [{"id": "gatikArakopapadAt‌ kft‌", "headword": "गतिकारकोपपदात्‌ कृत्‌", "headword_slp1": "gatikArakopapadAt‌ kft‌", "fold": "gatikarakopapadat‌ kft‌", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In a तत्-पुरुष समास a word ending in a कृत् affix preserves its original accent when preceded by an indeclinable called गति -- गतिश्च १.४.६०, or a noun standing in intimate relation to a verb (कारक) or any word which gives occasion for compounding (उपपद -- तत्रोपपदं सप्तमीस्थम्‌ ३.१.९२)\n\nTerms: समास end acute-2nd-term", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["